  ("How much does thermostat installation cost in Ontario?", "Thermostat installation cost depends on the thermostat and the wiring work, so EHI quotes a guaranteed price up front. A simple furnace thermostat replacement is a quick visit, while a smart thermostat with a new C-wire and heat pump configuration takes longer. A $100 rebate is available on qualifying smart thermostats through the Home Renovation Savings Program."),
  ("Is there a rebate for smart thermostats in Ontario?", "Yes. The Home Renovation Savings Program offers a $100 rebate on qualifying smart thermostats for eligible Ontario homes. EHI confirms eligibility before installation and handles the paperwork. Program terms can change, so check before you buy."),
  ("Do I need a C-wire for a smart thermostat?", "In most cases, yes. A smart thermostat needs continuous 24V power from a common (C) wire to run its display and Wi-Fi. If your existing cable has no spare wire, we run a new one or install a C-wire adapter at the furnace so the thermostat never drops offline."),
  ("What is the balance point on a heat pump thermostat?", "The balance point is the outdoor temperature below which the heat pump alone can no longer meet the heat loss of the house and backup heat, either electric auxiliary or a gas furnace, is allowed to help. Setting it correctly keeps auxiliary heat off until it is needed, which is the main thing that keeps heat pump hydro bills low."),
  ("Why is my auxiliary heat running so much?", "Auxiliary heat runs too often when the thermostat's balance point or auxiliary lockout is set too warm, when large setbacks make the thermostat call for a fast recovery, or when the thermostat is not configured for a heat pump at all. Correct configuration fixes it in most homes."),
